WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.934 --> 00:00:02.135
-Guys, it's hard to believe,

00:00:02.135 --> 00:00:04.337
but it's been over a year
since we all got on Zoom.

00:00:04.337 --> 00:00:06.539
And, yet, some people are still
getting the hang of it,

00:00:06.539 --> 00:00:07.540
even people on TV.

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:08.742
So you know what that means.

00:00:08.742 --> 00:00:10.409
It's time for another
installment of

00:00:10.409 --> 00:00:12.711
"Greatest Moments
in Zoom History."

00:00:12.711 --> 00:00:13.713
Enjoy.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:13.713 --> 00:00:17.250
♪♪

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:18.751 line:0%
-What do you think is
most important,

00:00:18.751 --> 00:00:21.087 line:0%
most urgent right now?

00:00:26.292 --> 00:00:31.898 line:0%
-We have also heard reports that
grant funding has gone down de--

00:00:33.666 --> 00:00:35.434 line:0%
-I think I lost
Representative Clark.

00:00:35.434 --> 00:00:38.337 line:0%
-I understand that
Congresswoman Clark is back on.

00:00:38.337 --> 00:00:41.107 line:0%
-I hope this is
a more successful outing.

00:00:41.107 --> 00:00:43.977 line:0%
We are seeing --

00:00:43.977 --> 00:00:46.012 line:0%
-Representative Gerry Connolly
of Virginia,

00:00:46.012 --> 00:00:49.615 line:0%
who's the president of the
NATO Parliamentary Assembly,

00:00:49.615 --> 00:00:51.284 line:0%
for five minutes.

00:00:51.284 --> 00:00:54.586 line:0%
-[ Indiscernible robotic voice ]

00:00:54.586 --> 00:00:56.889 line:0%
-We're having a hard
time hearing you, Mr. Connolly.

00:00:56.889 --> 00:00:58.157 line:0%
You're coming in --

00:00:58.157 --> 00:01:03.863 line:0%
You're breaking up.
It's hard to understand you.

00:01:03.863 --> 00:01:04.964 line:0%
-[ Robotic voice ]
Can you hear me now?

00:01:04.964 --> 00:01:07.600 line:0%
-It is unbelievable
what we're seeing.

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:10.403 line:0%
And -- And you're --
the quote by Bernie Sanders --

00:01:10.403 --> 00:01:14.440 line:0%
[ Echoing ]

00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:17.743 line:0%
-The gentleman is recognized
for five minutes.

00:01:17.743 --> 00:01:19.712 line:0%
-Today's gig economy
sprung out

00:01:19.712 --> 00:01:21.481 line:0%
from the last recession.

00:01:21.481 --> 00:01:23.582 line:0%
It offers a job to anyone
who wants one.

00:01:23.582 --> 00:01:27.019 line:0%
-Mr. Mfume, can you center your
mic or your computer

00:01:27.019 --> 00:01:28.587 line:0%
so we can see your face?

00:01:28.587 --> 00:01:31.290 line:0%
-I did not know, Madam Chair,
that you could not.

00:01:31.290 --> 00:01:33.192 line:0%
-I now call upon
the prime minister

00:01:33.192 --> 00:01:35.328 line:0%
of the Republic of India,
his excellency Narendra Modi.

00:01:35.328 --> 00:01:38.831 line:0%
-Your excellency,
President Biden.

00:01:38.831 --> 00:01:40.566 line:0%
[ Phone dialing ]

00:01:40.566 --> 00:01:44.036 line:0%
Colleagues.
My fellow citizens.

00:01:44.036 --> 00:01:45.037 line:0%
[ Phone dialing ]

00:01:45.037 --> 00:01:46.172 line:0%
-What made you want to do it?

00:01:46.172 --> 00:01:48.541 line:0%
-Well, my mom presented
the idea to me,

00:01:48.541 --> 00:01:52.745 line:0%
and she said that I could be
one of the first --

00:01:52.745 --> 00:01:54.246 line:0%
-I think we just lost Ty.

00:01:54.246 --> 00:01:57.517 line:0%
Ty, I think we have you back,
so I'll ask the question again.

00:01:57.517 --> 00:01:59.419 line:0%
What made you want to be
a part of this trial?

00:02:03.455 --> 00:02:06.392 line:0%
-And, John, in the early days
of this investigation,

00:02:06.392 --> 00:02:07.927 line:0%
what stands out to you the most?

00:02:07.927 --> 00:02:10.596 line:0%
-One-two, one-two, one-two,
one-two, one-two, one-two.

00:02:10.596 --> 00:02:14.300 line:0%
One, two, three, four, five --
-We can hear you, John.

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:17.336
-It's the most universal way
for all of us to stay active.

00:02:17.336 --> 00:02:19.072
How you doing, there,
Matt Titus?

00:02:22.909 --> 00:02:25.778 line:0%
-So, let's see if
we can give Theresa a call.

00:02:25.778 --> 00:02:26.946 line:0%
-Hello?!

00:02:26.946 --> 00:02:29.148 line:0%
-Theresa!
-Theresa!

00:02:29.148 --> 00:02:30.950 line:0%
-You're upside down, girl.

00:02:30.950 --> 00:02:33.486 line:0%
Will you flip
your phone upside down?

00:02:33.486 --> 00:02:34.921 line:0%
-We can't see you.
-This way?

00:02:34.921 --> 00:02:37.456 line:0%
-One more. One more click.
-One more.

00:02:37.456 --> 00:02:40.326 line:0%
One more. One more. One more.
-One more. One more.

00:02:40.326 --> 00:02:41.727 line:0%
Yeah!
-Yes!

00:02:41.727 --> 00:02:43.428 line:0%
-Okay, let's call Jackie.
-Okay. Here we go.

00:02:43.428 --> 00:02:44.530 line:0%
[ Video call ringing ]

00:02:44.530 --> 00:02:46.232 line:0%
-Hey -- Hi, Jackie.

00:02:46.232 --> 00:02:48.400 line:0%
How are you?
-Hi.

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:49.802 line:0%
-I'm great. How are you?

00:02:49.802 --> 00:02:51.237 line:0%
-There you are -- Oh --
-Flip it the other way.

00:02:51.237 --> 00:02:52.238 line:0%
-Just one more flip.

00:02:52.238 --> 00:02:54.140 line:0%
Oh, one more.

00:02:54.140 --> 00:02:55.575 line:0%
One more.
-One more flip.

00:02:55.575 --> 00:02:57.009 line:0%
-Just a half a flip.
Freeze, freeze.

00:02:57.009 --> 00:02:58.111 line:0%
-I love them both.

00:02:58.111 --> 00:02:59.612 line:0%
I hope it's true.
That would be awesome.

00:02:59.612 --> 00:03:00.947 line:0%
-Oh!
-Okay, good. Alright.

00:03:00.947 --> 00:03:02.414 line:0%
-We were just
saying the same thing.

00:03:02.414 --> 00:03:04.183 line:0%
-Oh, no.
-Oh, my gosh!

00:03:04.183 --> 00:03:06.519 line:0%
-Kelsey, good morning.

00:03:08.287 --> 00:03:10.356 line:0%
Oh, can we not hear him?
-Can you hear him?

00:03:10.356 --> 00:03:11.357 line:0%
-I can't hear him.
-I can't hear him either.

00:03:11.357 --> 00:03:14.760 line:0%
-Uh-oh. Are you on mute?

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:16.795 line:0%
-There we go.

00:03:16.795 --> 00:03:19.532 line:0%
-We had you for a second. Nope.

00:03:19.532 --> 00:03:21.568 line:0%
-[ Speaking native language ]

00:03:23.436 --> 00:03:27.140 line:0%
♪♪

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:29.175 line:0%
[ Speaking native language ]

00:03:31.243 --> 00:03:33.580 line:0%
-Kits do it --
YouTube kits do it,

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:36.950 line:0%
and the BBC are also now
embracing this.

00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:39.385 line:0%
Why -- I apologize for
my cat's tail.

00:03:39.385 --> 00:03:41.787 line:0%
Why are you...

00:03:41.787 --> 00:03:44.056 line:0%
-It's important to have
those protections in place

00:03:44.056 --> 00:03:45.625 line:0%
for everybody.

00:03:59.772 --> 00:04:01.841 line:0%
-Mnh-mnh. Uh --

00:04:01.841 --> 00:04:03.342 line:0%
-I think I -- Did I lose you?

00:04:03.342 --> 00:04:05.378
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:11.316 --> 00:04:12.885
-"Um -- Uh -- "

